> pathname <- getPathname(cdf)
> pathname
[1] "C:/Documents and Settings/hb/My Documents/My Data/annotationData/chipTypes/
MoEx-1_0-st-v1/MoEx-1_0-st-v1.cdf"
> cells <- readCdfCellIndices(pathname, units=654123)
> cells
$`4987965`
$`4987965`$groups
$`4987965`$groups$`4987965`
$`4987965`$groups$`4987965`$indices
[1] 3562470 1875619 4773230 2131705
> gc()
          used (Mb) gc trigger (Mb) max used (Mb)
Ncells 1172035 31.3    1368491 36.6  1265230 33.8
Vcells  476127  3.7     905753  7.0   786244  6.0

In other words, you should expect it to work.  Note also that the
above hardly uses any memory, so that is not the reason for the crash.

More troubleshooting:

1) Verify that you get the same checksum as I do. Do you?

2) Start a fresh R session, and load just package affxparser.  Then retry:
      cells <- readCdfCellIndices(pathname, units=1)
      cells <- readCdfCellIndices(pathname, units=654123)
    Does it crash?

3) What is your absolute/full pathname of the CDF?
      print(pathname)
      print(getAbsolutePath(pathname))

4) Try also:
      cells <- readCdfCellIndices(getAbsolutePath(pathname), units=1)
      ...
5) ..., as well as:
      setwd(dirname(pathname))
      cells <- readCdfCellIndices("MoEx-1_0-st-v1.cdf", units=1)
      ...

6) BTW, does the above work for any other CDFs?  Is this the CDF you
try?  Maybe we at least can out rule the CDF per se.

7) Try also to reinstall 'affxparser'.

Any differences?

/H

