> > 3) Above it says the CDF is 740.05MB.  This is so large so I suspect you
> have an ASCII version of the CDF.  You will be much much much^10 better
> off if you work with a binary CDF instead.  The IO will be many times
> faster.  This could also explain the slow performance on Unix. It might
> also explain why it crashes on Windows; affxparser/Fusion SDK may simply
> run out of memory.  You can convert a CDF from ASCII to binary, using
> convertCdf() in the affxparser package.  See ?convertCdf for more
> details.  Archive the ASCII version somewhere and replace it with new
> binary CDF.  When you do print(cdf) on the new CDF, you should see that
> the file size is much smaller, around 50-80 MB.
> >
